{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20242",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.34,
      "end_seconds": 5.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Hi, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.5,
      "end_seconds": 10.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.92,
      "end_seconds": 21.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.94,
      "text": "Well, I've been having wheezing when I exercise. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.56,
      "end_seconds": 26.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.51,
      "end_seconds": 30.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "It's been about a month now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.56,
      "end_seconds": 36.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.99,
      "end_seconds": 46.02,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "I'd call it severe. It's every other day. It settles a little with my inhaler and resting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.81,
      "end_seconds": 51.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Any a cough at night as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.3,
      "end_seconds": 73.37,
      "duration_seconds": 21.07,
      "text": "Yes, actually. Hmm, as for cough at night, honestly, a couple of times a week. And there's chest tightness as well, um, one week now. With chest tightness, it happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.09,
      "end_seconds": 86.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Have you noticed weight loss, chest pain or blue lips?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.75,
      "end_seconds": 94.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "Let me think, no weight loss, chest pain or blue lips, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.17,
      "end_seconds": 98.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.44,
      "end_seconds": 103.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I mean, no, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.59,
      "end_seconds": 116.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.55,
      "end_seconds": 131.09,
      "duration_seconds": 11.54,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.65,
      "end_seconds": 134.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.24,
      "end_seconds": 142.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "Hmm, I had a mole taken off my arm a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.95,
      "end_seconds": 148.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.54,
      "end_seconds": 153.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Foracort inhaler. I take it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.41,
      "end_seconds": 156.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.16,
      "end_seconds": 162.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "For nearly five years. I'm on hydrocortisone cream, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.1,
      "end_seconds": 171.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.42,
      "end_seconds": 179.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.34,
      "end_seconds": 182.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.61,
      "end_seconds": 187.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.19,
      "end_seconds": 192.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.26,
      "end_seconds": 196.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.48,
      "end_seconds": 203.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.46,
      "end_seconds": 208.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.79,
      "end_seconds": 213.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.76,
      "end_seconds": 224.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "I've got asthma. Mm, I've had eczema, yes. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.69,
      "end_seconds": 233.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Alright, asthma, that matches what I have here. Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.0,
      "end_seconds": 242.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.62,
      "end_seconds": 273.59,
      "duration_seconds": 10.97,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 98 percent, temperature is 37.0 degrees. And respiratory rate 16, pressure 114 over 81, pulse is 69 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.05,
      "end_seconds": 277.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.28,
      "end_seconds": 282.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.16,
      "end_seconds": 288.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.6,
      "end_seconds": 291.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.98,
      "end_seconds": 293.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.11,
      "end_seconds": 308.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "I can hear a faint wheeze at the end of breathing out, otherwise the chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.98,
      "end_seconds": 311.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.99,
      "end_seconds": 327.54,
      "duration_seconds": 11.55,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Okay, so my impression is this: The most likely explanation is exercise-triggered asthma with seasonal allergy. Another possibility is a viral chest infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.72,
      "end_seconds": 331.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Uh, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.94,
      "end_seconds": 356.63,
      "duration_seconds": 23.69,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's exercise-triggered asthma with seasonal allergy, and we'll know more once the an allergy test is back. So, to recap quickly. You've had wheezing when you exercise for about a month, severe, and no blue lips or weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.43,
      "end_seconds": 360.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.2,
      "end_seconds": 392.59,
      "duration_seconds": 30.39,
      "text": "I'm going to order an allergy test, for seasonal symptoms. I want a peak flow diary done, that's for asthma. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'm going to order a breathing test, for wheeze. Rinse your mouth after the preventer inhaler and use the spacer. One warning sign to remember: the inhaler isn't helping or you cannot speak in full sentences. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.75,
      "end_seconds": 400.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the breathing test. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.48,
      "end_seconds": 407.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.18,
      "end_seconds": 409.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}